---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Experience | William Schibler">
<section class="page-hero experience-hero info-page-hero">   <div class="page-container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Experience</p>
      <h1>Technical work, leadership, and hands-on responsibility.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section experience-list">
    <article class="experience experience-card experience-card--rocket">
      <div class="experience-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg
          class="experience-icon lucide-icon"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path
            class="icon-main"
            d="M12 15v5s3.03-.55 4-2c1.08-1.62 0-5 0-5"
          />
          <path
            class="icon-accent"
            d="M4.5 16.5c-1.5 1.26-2 5-2 5s3.74-.5 5-2c.71-.84.7-2.13-.09-2.91a2.18 2.18 0 0 0-2.91-.09"
          />
          <path
            class="icon-main"
            d="M9 12a22 22 0 0 1 2-3.95A12.88 12.88 0 0 1 22 2c0 2.72-.78 7.5-6 11a22.4 22.4 0 0 1-4 2z"
          />
          <path
            class="icon-main"
            d="M9 12H4s.55-3.03 2-4c1.62-1.08 5 .05 5 .05"
          />
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="experience-content">
        <div class="experience-meta">
          <p class="eyebrow">NU Aerospace: Liquid Rocket Engine</p>
          <span>September 2025 – Present</span>
        </div>

        <h2>Project Leader and Contributor</h2>

        <details class="experience-details">
          <summary>View details</summary>
          <div class="experience-details-content">
            <p>
              Since joining AerospaceNU's Liquid Rocket Engine Team at Northeastern
              University, I have been able to contribute to the team's efforts and
              learn a lot from their veteran members. Following their introductory
              program that taught the fundamentals of how their bipropellant liquid
              rocket engine functions, I showed up every day looking for opportunities
              to learn and contribute. Through that interest, I have supported
              test-stand assembly, pressurized water-flow testing, and the fabrication
              of components for the test stand, among several other responsibilities.
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                Measured out, modeled, selected materials for, machined, and installed
                components onto the team's test stand.
              </li>
              <li>
                Assisted in pressurized water-flow testing of the fluid systems at
                pressures ranging from 600 to 1,000 psig.
              </li>
              <li>
                Currently co-leading a small team to create a custom cryogenic
                capacitive fill-level sensor for the team's liquid-oxygen tank.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <a class="text-link" href="/projects/nitrogen-tank-holder/">
              Related hardware project →
            </a>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="experience experience-card experience-card--seattle">
      <div class="experience-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg
          class="experience-icon lucide-icon"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path
            class="icon-main"
            d="M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h5a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v15a3 3 0 0 0-3-3Z"
          />
          <path
            class="icon-main"
            d="M21 18a1 1 0 0 0 1-1V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-5a3 3 0 0 0-3 3v15a3 3 0 0 1 3-3Z"
          />
          <path class="icon-accent" d="M12 6v15" />
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="experience-content">
        <div class="experience-meta">
          <p class="eyebrow">Seattle Summer-In NU Program</p>
          <span>May 2026 – June 2026</span>
        </div>

        <h2>Student</h2>

        <details class="experience-details">
          <summary>View details</summary>
          <div class="experience-details-content">
  <p>
    I spent half of my 2026 summer in Seattle completing coursework for
    my Aerospace Engineering minor. My classes integrated concepts from
    thermodynamics and fluid mechanics to explain the fundamentals of
    lift, drag, airfoil design, and aircraft-engine operation. I applied
    these concepts through multiple projects using MATLAB and computational
    fluid dynamics. Beyond the classroom, the program included tours of an
    operating wind tunnel, visits to Hawaiian Airlines and Alaska Airlines,
    and aerospace-industry alumni panels, among other experiences.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      Simulated a Titan atmospheric gas mixture through a single-stage
      axial compressor in ANSYS Fluent as part of a team of three.
    </li>
    <li>
      Studied the fundamentals of airfoil design, aerodynamic performance,
      and lift and drag generation.
    </li>
    <li>
      Applied governing equations to model the operation and performance
      of turbojet-engine systems.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <a class="text-link" href="/projects/titan-axial-compressor/">
    Related compressor project →
  </a>
</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="experience experience-card experience-card--makerspace">
      <div class="experience-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg
          class="experience-icon lucide-icon"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path
            class="icon-main"
            d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.106-3.105c.32-.322.863-.22.983.218a6 6 0 0 1-8.259 7.057l-7.91 7.91a1 1 0 0 1-2.999-3l7.91-7.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.057-8.259c.438.12.54.662.219.984z"
          />
          <circle class="icon-accent-fill" cx="5.15" cy="18.85" r="1.05" />
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="experience-content">
        <div class="experience-meta">
          <p class="eyebrow">Northeastern Makerspace</p>
          <span>September 2025 – Present</span>
        </div>

        <h2>Explorer and MIG Welding Trainer</h2>

        <details class="experience-details">
          <summary>View details</summary>
          <div class="experience-details-content">
            <p>
              At the EXP Makerspace at Northeastern University, I regularly assist
              students and faculty with a wide range of needs, including
              troubleshooting equipment, advising patrons on projects, and leading
              orientations. The role requires me to be adaptable and capable of
              learning how to operate and repair unfamiliar machines in the moment.
              Beyond helping run the space, staff members can qualify to lead
              equipment trainings. I currently teach MIG welding and am completing
              qualifications to teach CNC Tormach machining, TIG welding, and
              waterjet cutting.
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                Train novice patrons in MIG welding on a weekly basis.
              </li>
              <li>
                Troubleshoot and repair equipment such as 3D printers, laser
                cutters, sewing machines, and soldering stations, among other
                machines.
              </li>
              <li>
                Lead hour-long makerspace orientations for groups ranging from one
                person to more than thirty participants.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="experience experience-card experience-card--maze">
      <div class="experience-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg
          class="experience-icon lucide-icon"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <circle class="icon-accent" cx="6" cy="19" r="3" />
          <path
            class="icon-main"
            d="M9 19h8.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0-7h-11a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0-7H15"
          />
          <circle class="icon-accent-secondary" cx="18" cy="5" r="3" />
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="experience-content">
        <div class="experience-meta">
          <p class="eyebrow">STEM Game for Children</p>
          <span>February 2025 – April 2025</span>
        </div>

        <h2>Team Lead and Builder</h2>

        <details class="experience-details">
          <summary>View details</summary>
          <div class="experience-details-content">
            <p>
              For my Cornerstone of Engineering course at Northeastern University's
              Oakland campus, I was randomly assigned to a team of four engineering
              students and tasked with developing a STEM toy for a local school using
              the engineering design process. The four-month project involved
              conducting research, brainstorming concepts, building prototypes,
              delegating responsibilities, resolving team disagreements, and
              gathering feedback from the intended users. The work was divided into
              multiple phases, with different team members serving as leaders
              throughout the project.
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                Designed and built an interactive magnetic marble maze for children.
              </li>
              <li>
                Contributed through woodworking, 3D modeling, 3D printing,
                electronics, and embedded programming.
              </li>
              <li>
                Led and contributed to multiple project phases while tracking
                progress toward project goals and managing the team's time.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <a class="text-link" href="/projects/magnetic-marble-maze/">
              Related project →
            </a>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="experience experience-card experience-card--lab">
      <div class="experience-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg
          class="experience-icon lucide-icon"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path
            class="icon-main"
            d="M14 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 .245.96l5.51 10.08A2 2 0 0 1 18 22H6a2 2 0 0 1-1.755-2.96l5.51-10.08A2 2 0 0 0 10 8V2"
          />
          <path class="icon-accent" d="M6.453 15h11.094" />
          <path class="icon-main" d="M8.5 2h7" />
          <circle class="icon-accent-fill" cx="9" cy="18" r=".75" />
          <circle class="icon-accent-fill" cx="14.8" cy="18.8" r=".55" />
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="experience-content">
        <div class="experience-meta">
          <p class="eyebrow">Bioengineering Wet-Lab Work</p>
          <span>September 2025 – December 2025</span>
        </div>

        <h2>Student</h2>

        <details class="experience-details">
          <summary>View details</summary>
          <div class="experience-details-content">
  <p>
    During my bioengineering coursework at Northeastern University, I
    learned to use MATLAB to analyze large datasets, calculate probability
    and statistical measures, and identify correlations among variables. I
    applied these skills through both computational modeling and wet-lab
    experimentation, such as live/dead cell-assay analysis, exploration of
    SIR models, and interpretation of enzyme reaction rates using gel
    electrophoresis.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      Manipulated and analyzed biological materials in a sterile wet-lab
      environment.
    </li>
    <li>
      Created MATLAB code for simulations and data analysis to identify
      relationships between experimental variables.
    </li>
    <li>
      Developed hypotheses from research, interpreted experimental results,
      and communicated conclusions in an effective and professional manner.
    </li>
  </ul>

</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="experience experience-card experience-card--leadership">
      <div class="experience-visual" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg
          class="experience-icon lucide-icon leadership-icon"
          viewBox="0 0 24 26"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path
            class="icon-accent-fill"
            d="m12 1.3 1.08 2.2 2.42.35-1.75 1.7.41 2.41L12 6.83 9.84 7.96l.41-2.41-1.75-1.7 2.42-.35L12 1.3Z"
          />
          <g class="icon-main" transform="translate(0 4)">
            <path d="M18 21a8 8 0 0 0-16 0" />
            <circle cx="10" cy="8" r="5" />
            <path d="M22 20c0-3.37-2-6.5-4-8a5 5 0 0 0-.45-8.3" />
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="experience-content">
        <div class="experience-meta">
          <p class="eyebrow">Makerspace Club</p>
          <span>February 2025 – April 2025</span>
        </div>

        <h2>Founder and President</h2>

        <details class="experience-details">
          <summary>View details</summary>
          <div class="experience-details-content">
            <p>
              At Northeastern University's Oakland campus, I co-founded a club to
              promote the newly established makerspaces. The club's purpose was to
              raise student awareness of the available resources and encourage
              students from all majors to explore their creativity. During one
              semester, our team established the club, organized seven events in
              twelve weeks, and received an award for hosting the best club event of
              the year, as voted on by the Student Involvement staff.
            </p>

            <ul>
              <li>
                Hosted events featuring activities created with makerspace equipment
                such as 3D printers, laser cutters, and vinyl cutters, among other
                machines.
              </li>
              <li>
                Coordinated communication with club advisors, sponsors, executive
                board members, and general club members.
              </li>
              <li>
                Received recognition for hosting the best club event of the year, as
                voted on by the Student Involvement staff.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>

.experience-hero {
  border-bottom: 0;
}

  .experience-list {
    --experience-gap: 28px;
    --icon-panel-height: 176px;
    position: relative;
    gap: var(--experience-gap);
    padding-left: 58px;
  }

  .experience-card {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 120px minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: 20px;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: visible;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 0;
    background: transparent;
  }

  .experience-card::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: calc(var(--icon-panel-height) / 2);
    left: -43px;
    z-index: 2;
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    border: 4px solid var(--bg);
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(31, 95, 174, 0.35);
    transform: translateY(-50%);
  }

  .experience-card:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: calc(var(--icon-panel-height) / 2);
    left: -32px;
    z-index: 1;
    width: 2px;
    height: calc(100% + var(--experience-gap));
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      rgba(31, 95, 174, 0.82),
      rgba(31, 95, 174, 0.32)
    );
  }

  .experience-visual {
    display: grid;
    height: var(--icon-panel-height);
    place-items: center;
    padding: 24px 20px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, var(--panel-start), var(--panel-end));
    box-shadow:
      0 12px 26px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.16),
      0 3px 8px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.08);
    transition:
      transform 180ms ease,
      box-shadow 180ms ease;
  }

  .experience-icon {
    width: 72px;
    height: 72px;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .experience-icon path,
  .experience-icon circle {
    fill: none;
    stroke-width: 3;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .experience-icon .icon-main {
    stroke: #ffffff;
  }

  .experience-icon .icon-accent {
    stroke: var(--icon-accent);
  }

  .experience-icon.lucide-icon path,
  .experience-icon.lucide-icon circle {
    stroke-width: 1.8;
  }

  .experience-icon .icon-accent-secondary {
    stroke: var(--icon-accent-secondary, var(--icon-accent));
  }

  .experience-icon .icon-accent-fill {
    fill: var(--icon-accent);
    stroke: none;
  }

  .experience-icon .icon-main path,
  .experience-icon .icon-main circle {
    stroke: #ffffff;
  }

  .experience-content {
    min-width: 0;
    min-height: var(--icon-panel-height);
    padding: 24px 30px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow:
      0 12px 28px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.11),
      0 3px 8px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.05);
    transition:
      transform 180ms ease,
      border-color 180ms ease,
      box-shadow 180ms ease;
  }

  .experience-card:hover .experience-visual,
  .experience-card:hover .experience-content {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .experience-card:hover .experience-content {
    border-color: rgba(31, 95, 174, 0.58);
    box-shadow:
      0 18px 38px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.15),
      0 5px 12px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.07);
  }

  .experience-card:hover .experience-visual {
    box-shadow:
      0 16px 32px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.2),
      0 4px 10px rgba(8, 31, 57, 0.1);
  }

  .experience-meta {
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .experience-meta .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .experience-meta span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .experience-content h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .experience-card--rocket {
    --panel-start: #071f43;
    --panel-end: #123f78;
    --icon-accent: #5bc8ff;
  }

  .experience-card--seattle {
    --panel-start: #183d73;
    --panel-end: #2f6fb3;
    --icon-accent: #9edcff;
  }

  .experience-card--makerspace {
    --panel-start: #12489f;
    --panel-end: #2371dd;
    --icon-accent: #ffd166;
  }

  .experience-card--maze {
    --panel-start: #0f3567;
    --panel-end: #1b579d;
    --icon-accent: #8fe3ff;
    --icon-accent-secondary: #ffc857;
  }

  .experience-card--lab {
    --panel-start: #17445f;
    --panel-end: #287b95;
    --icon-accent: #7ce2c5;
  }

  .experience-card--leadership {
    --panel-start: #24396d;
    --panel-end: #385a9d;
    --icon-accent: #ffc857;
  }

  .experience-details {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .experience-details summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 820;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .experience-details summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

.experience-details summary::after {
  content: "";
  width: 36px;
  height: 36px;
  flex: 0 0 36px;

  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 50%;

  background:
    linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 14px 4px no-repeat,
    linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 4px 14px no-repeat;
}

.experience-details[open] summary::after {
  background:
    linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 14px 2px no-repeat;
}

  .experience-details-content {
    padding-top: 20px;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }

  .experience-details-content p {
  text-align: justify;
}

  .experience-details-content > :first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .experience-details-content > :last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .experience-details-content .text-link {
    display: inline-block;
  }
  
  @media (min-width: 1181px) {
  /* Experience hero scaled to match the compact Projects-page proportions. */

  /* Overall Experience-page frame and entry spacing. */

  .experience-list {
    --experience-gap: 24px;
    --icon-panel-height: 140px;

    width: min(calc(100% - 72px), 1140px);
    gap: var(--experience-gap);
    padding-block: 76px;
    padding-left: 52px;
  }

  .experience-card {
    grid-template-columns: 96px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
  }

  /* Timeline marker and connector. */

  .experience-card::before {
    left: -39px;
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    border-width: 3px;
  }

  .experience-card:not(:last-child)::after {
    left: -30px;
  }

  /* Fixed colored icon panel. */

  .experience-visual {
    height: var(--icon-panel-height);
    padding: 18px 16px;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .experience-icon {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
  }

  /* White experience content card. */

  .experience-content {
    min-height: var(--icon-panel-height);
    padding: 18px 24px;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }

  .experience-meta {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .experience-meta .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .experience-meta span {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .experience-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  /* View-details row and plus/minus control. */

  .experience-details {
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding-top: 10px;
  }

  .experience-details summary {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .experience-details summary::after {
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
    flex-basis: 30px;

    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 12px 3px no-repeat,
      linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 3px 12px no-repeat;
  }

  .experience-details[open] summary::after {
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent)) center / 12px 2px no-repeat;
  }

  /* Expanded description, bullets, and related-project link. */

  .experience-details-content {
    padding-top: 16px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .experience-details-content ul {
    margin-block: 16px;
    padding-left: 1.35rem;
  }

  .experience-details-content li + li {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }

  .experience-details-content .text-link {
    padding-top: 12px;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
}

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .experience-list {
      gap: 22px;
      padding-left: 0;
    }

    .experience-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .experience-card::before,
    .experience-card::after {
      display: none;
    }

    .experience-visual {
      height: 104px;
      padding: 18px;
    }

    .experience-icon {
      width: 64px;
      height: 64px;
    }

    .experience-content {
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .experience-card:hover .experience-visual,
    .experience-card:hover .experience-content {
      transform: none;
    }
  }
</style>
